package io.github.jimbozoomer.jugcraft.menagerie;

import io.github.jimbozoomer.jugcraft.guide.encyclopedia.PageWriter;
import net.minecraft.network.chat.Component;

/** Player instructions for the implemented household interactions, with no research requirement. */
final class OwnerSupplementGuide {
    private OwnerSupplementGuide(){}
    static void write(PageWriter out){
        out.heading(Component.literal("Letters, drawings and announcements"));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Craft a wooden sign into two direction signs. Use one on the upper or lower half of a fence or wall post to attach a board while retaining the original post, or place one on a solid wall. Empty-hand use edits the clicked board, and a copper wrench turns it by 22.5 degrees. Dyes and glow ink style the lettering; honeycomb protects it and an axe removes the coating. Crouch-use shears to recover one board; removing the last restores the post. Breaking the post returns its material and both attached signs."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Use an empty hand on a blackboard to draw, erase, undo or copy a design. Save applies it to the board. Dyes draw directly on its face; glow ink lights the drawing. Honeycomb protects it from edits; an axe removes that coating. Soap clears an unwaxed drawing."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("The woven doormat opens a three-line lettering editor from its top. Its side hides one item: use an item to tuck it beneath, then use an empty hand on the side or crouch to retrieve it. Dyes, glow ink and wax also work on its lettering."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("A speaker lets you set a message, display style and range. A rising redstone signal announces it to nearby players. It waits five seconds between announcements; multiple speakers also share a short listener cooldown. Narrator mode respects the listener's accessibility setting."));
        out.heading(Component.literal("Display your collection"));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Barnacles grow on solid underwater surfaces along beaches and ocean floors in newly explored terrain. Silk Touch collects one per occupied face; bone meal spreads them underwater where you have building permission. Flax seeds also fit in an ordinary flower pot. Craft a jar with a boat to make the original rocking ship-in-a-bottle decoration."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Wandering traders sell globes for 10 emeralds and sepia globes for 12. Use one to spin it and read your coordinates; redstone pulses spin it too. A comparator reads 15 while spinning, then 1–4 for its stopped face. Shears toggle the cutaway view. Rename a globe in an anvil, or apply a named name tag, to select supplied designs such as Moon, Sun or Flat Earth. Names and the cutaway survive picking it up."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Crouch-use a book against a surface to place a pile. Use more books to add up to four, then an empty hand to take the clicked book back. Text and enchantments stay with each book. Ordinary books placed against a side can stand upright. Nearby piles contribute enchanting power when the route to the table is clear."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Give a statue one item to pose with it. Crouch-use to take it back; a redstone signal makes the statue wave. Candles light its display. A goblet holds a potion, milk or honey. Pour a drink in, use an empty hand to drink, or supply the matching empty bottle/bucket to take it away."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Flags copy a same-colored banner's patterns in a crafting grid; the patterned source is returned. Place sticks vertically to make a pole, then use an empty hand on its flag to raise it one section, or crouch-use to lower it. Patterns and custom names travel with the flag."));
        out.heading(Component.literal("Small improvements to familiar blocks"));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Place carpet on a bottom slab or stair to cover it without replacing its material. Dye recolors the carpet; shears lift it off and restore the original block. Put a tool on an unused tripwire hook to display it, then take it back with an empty hand. Attached tripwire mechanisms are left working."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Flower pots can hang beneath a solid support or chain; add a normal pottable plant and retrieve it with an empty hand. Place a lantern against a wall or post to use its matching bracket. Lily pads can support carpets, candles, lanterns and flower pots; the pad moves into its water cell and returns to the surface when the decoration is removed. Use a connected chain to ring a bell up to sixteen blocks away."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("A second cake placed on an untouched cake makes a double cake with fourteen servings. The upper cake is eaten first. Cakes face the side from which you begin eating."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Dye a water cauldron to make a dye bath. Colors can mix; glass bottles collect a layer of dye. Dye bottles recolor equipment or familiar colored building blocks in crafting, returning the glass bottle. A cauldron layer dyes four individual items. Pour normal potions into an empty cauldron to store three bottles; compatible effects mix with dilution and an eight-effect limit. Instant effects cannot be mixed with different potions. Each potion layer tips two batches of eight arrows, or fills one bottle. You can also toss those dyeable items or arrow batches into the bath; one batch is processed each second while its thrower is online and permitted. A water bucket discards the mixture and refills the cauldron with water."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Hang banners from a ceiling to keep their patterns on a swaying cloth. Two skulls can stack in one block; add up to four matching candles to a skull and light them with flint and steel. Empty-hand use extinguishes them; crouch-use removes the candles. Player-head profiles are retained."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Use fire charges in the air to throw them; strike a flying charge to deflect it. Sneak-use binds a charge stack for dispenser launching while you are online and permitted. Craft a dragon charge from obsidian, dragon's breath and gunpowder for a short, expanding breath cloud. These effects respect combat protection and do not destroy terrain. Snowball hits build up freezing; a successful direct hit with a torch ignites the target briefly."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Crouch-use an empty hand on a lectern with a writable book to edit or sign it in place. Crouch-use an item on either face of a hanging sign to display it; an empty hand retrieves it. Text is preserved underneath. Wax prevents changes. Detached lanterns fall and settle where allowed, or drop as items; they never start fires. A lit campfire, magma or another tagged heat source makes water, dye and potion cauldrons bubble. Boiling liquid is hazardous outside protected land."));
        out.heading(Component.literal("Practical workshop details"));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Add rods from another face to cross them in one block; breaking the crossing returns its separate rods. Rope connects to supports and nearby rope. Use more rope to extend a hanging line, an empty hand to retrieve its bottom segment, or shears to shorten the loose end. Vertical rope can be climbed. With animals already on your leads, use the rope to tether them to it; crouch to retrieve rope instead."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Craft an arrow with rope to make a rope arrow, then add more rope in crafting or by clicking rope onto the arrow in your inventory. It holds 32 paid ropes and unwinds one segment per tick after hitting an allowed attachment. Extra multishot arrows cannot create rope. Use a bow or crossbow; anonymous dispenser shots do not build in the world."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Buntings come in sixteen colors. Place them against a wall or beneath a ceiling, or click a connected horizontal rope branch to decorate that branch. Each of its four directions can hold a separate color. Use an empty hand on the branch to take its bunting back. Removed connections return their decorations."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Bellows blow along their facing direction. Use one by hand or supply redstone; airflow can move entities and accelerate an adjacent furnace while still consuming normal fuel. Spring launchers need an empty space in front and launch permitted entities when powered. Protected land and combat rules still apply."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("A copper wrench rotates a permitted single block around the clicked face; crouching reverses its direction. It also turns armor stands. Repair it with copper. Turntables rotate their facing neighbor with redstone: stronger signals turn faster. Matching tall two-part blocks rotate together. Standing on a powered upward turntable turns you too; crouch to opt out. Straight rails also reorient unoccupied carts. Linked machines and other unsupported assemblies must be repositioned with their own tools."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("The grouper compares the blocks on its left and right: 15 for identical states, 7 for the same block with different states, 0 otherwise. If both sides are open, it compares nearby entities instead, including dropped item components and animal variants."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Bamboo spikes face the surface they are placed against. A lingering potion coats them for up to sixteen successful effect applications; soap washes the coating off. Spikes keep their remaining coating when collected. Damage uses the owner's combat permissions and pauses while the owner is absent."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Hold a bamboo flute to play its supplied songs and recall your nearby companions. Use it on an owned tame animal or horse to bind up to six; crouch-use that animal to remove its binding. Bound pets must be loaded and within 128 blocks; an unbound flute calls up to sixteen nearby, standing pets within 32 blocks. Claims and safe landing space are respected. Rename the flute to a song name to select it; bamboo repairs it."));
        out.fact(Component.literal("Use the altimeter to read your elevation. Its original colored scale moves with your height and changes for the Overworld, Nether and End. Party poppers fire confetti; craft one with up to eight dyes to choose its colors, crouch-place confetti on a floor, or wear it as a party hat. Use one on an unignited creeper to give it a harmless confetti burst instead of an explosion."));
    }
}
